<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Perdiccas I of Macedon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perdiccas">Perdiccas</a> I is named by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> as the founder of the Argead royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> in the 7th century BCE. Herodotus tells how he and his brothers, exiles from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, came to Macedonia and won the kingship; later writers added earlier kings such as Caranus. His historicity is uncertain, but he heads the traditional king list of Macedon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/perdiccas-i-of-macedon.jpg" alt="Perdiccas I of Macedon" width="320" height="146" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aegae_-_Old_Macedonia_founded_by_Perdikkas_I_pre_500_BCE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
